                    (1, "body", "The yere of o[ur] lorde god: 1564: was the coldist springe & the wyndyst that eu[er] I did see / it was the gathyrist yere of blossings of", "The year of our Lord God 1564 was the coldest spring and the windiest that ever I did see; it was the gayest [most abundant] year of blossoms of", "Written upside-down relative to the main volume."),
                    (2, "body", "all man[ner] of frutte tres / and gret plenty of frute and the most p[ar]te of apples did ryse in the wynt[er] followynge by reson of y[e] frost hit", "all manner of fruit trees, and great plenty of fruit, and the most part of apples did rot/rise in the winter following by reason of the frost; it", ""),
                    (3, "body", "was so vehement / allso the sund & the aben[ing?] wynt[er] were very wyndy / & end was ffen", "was so vehement; also the summer and the winter were very windy, and [the] end was fair/fen.", ""),
                    (4, "body", "Mense Januarij: Si toni[truum] sonat: ventos validos: habundancia frug[um] adesse significant.", "In the month of January: If thunder sounds, it signifies strong winds and abundance of crops to be at hand.", "Latin thunder prognostication (Brontologium)."),
                    (5, "body", "Mense februarij: Si toni[truum] sonat: m[u]ltor[um] homi[n]um: maxie diuitu[m]: morbo interitu[m] adesse p[ro]nunciat.", "In the month of February: If thunder sounds, it announces that death by disease of many men, especially of the rich, is at hand.", ""),
                    (6, "body", "Mense Marcij: Si toni[truum]: ve[n]tos validos et copiam frug[um]: et lites in populo significat.", "In the month of March: If thunder [sounds], it signifies strong winds and plenty of crops, and strifes among the people.", ""),
                    (7, "body", "Mense Aprilis: Si toni[truum] sonat: an[num] iocundu[m] et fructuosu[m] ex om[n]ib[us] reb[us] denu[n]ciat: s[ed] inq[ui]or[um] hom[inum] morte[m] designat.", "In the month of April: If thunder sounds, it announces a pleasant and fruitful year in all things, but marks the death of wicked men.", ""),
                    (8, "body", "Mense Maij: Si toni[truum]: sonat Inopiam et famem in eo an[n]o afferre significat.", "In the month of May: If thunder sounds, it signifies that it brings scarcity and famine in that year.", ""),
                    (9, "body", "Mense Junij: Si toni[truum] sonat: homines diuites et pauperes et ligna siluar[um] p[er]iclitabuntur.", "In the month of June: If thunder sounds, rich and poor men and the trees of the woods shall be endangered.", ""),
                    (10, "body", "Mense Julij: Si toni[truum] sonat bona erit in illo Anno Annona.", "In the month of July: If thunder sounds, there shall be a good harvest in that year.", ""),
                    (11, "body", "Mense Augusti: Si toni[truum] sonat: habundancia frugum et occisionem potentu[m] significat.", "In the month of August: If thunder sounds, it signifies abundance of crops and the slaying of mighty men.", ""),
                    (12, "body", "Mense Septebri[s] Si toni[truum] sonat: habu[n]da[n]cia[m] frug[um] et occisione[m] pote[n]tu[m] signif[icat] et dol[orem] p[ro]nu[n]ciat p[ri]m[um].", "In the month of September: If thunder sounds, it signifies abundance of crops and the slaying of mighty men, and first announces grief.", ""),
                    (13, "body", "Mense Octobri Si toni[truum] sonat: ve[n]tos validos et an[n]ona[m] bonam et fenu[m] inopia[m] p[ro]nonciat.", "In the month of October: If thunder sounds, it announces strong winds and a good corn-harvest, and scarcity of hay.", ""),
                    (14, "body", "Mense Nouemb[ris] Si toni[truum] sonat: habundancia frug[um] et iocu[n]ditate[m] et om[n]ia p[ro]sp[er]a significat.", "In the month of November: If thunder sounds, it signifies abundance of crops and joyfulness and all prosperous things.", ""),
                    (15, "body", "Mense Decemb[ris]: Si toni[truum] sonat: Annona[m] bona[m] pace[m] int[er] gentes et om[n]ia p[ro]sp[er]a significat ess[e].", "In the month of December: If thunder sounds, it signifies a good harvest, peace among nations, and that all things are prosperous.", ""),
                    (16, "body", "¶ Si vent[us] fuit in prima nocte natalis d[omi]ni validus. in illo ano reges: principes et pontifices ceteriq[ue] diuites et pote[n]tes p[er] vni=", "If the wind was strong on the first night of the Nativity of the Lord, in that year kings, princes, and bishops, and other rich and mighty men throughout", "Red pilcrow '¶' at start."),
                    (17, "body", "uersu[m] orbe[m] p[er]ibunt. Si in: ij. nocte homi[nes] p[er] omnem orbe[m] deficient. Si in: iij. nocte in illo ano orphani et mulieres multe morie[n]t[ur]", "the whole world shall perish. If on the 2nd night, men throughout the whole world shall fail. If on the 3rd night, in that year orphans and many women shall die.", ""),
                    (18, "body", "Si in: iiij. nocte in illo ano panis no[n] abu[n]dabit. Si in: v. nocte artifices p[er]ibunt. Si in: vj. nocte in illo ano multa scandala adesse", "If on the 4th night, in that year bread shall not abound. If on the 5th night, craftsmen shall perish. If on the 6th night, in that year many scandals", ""),
                    (19, "body", "significat. Si in: vij. nocte in illo ano reges et pri[n]cipes et pontifices ad bellu[m] ibu[n]t et no[n] p[er]ibu[n]t sed sano inde redibu[n]t postea", "it signifies to be at hand. If on the 7th night, in that year kings and princes and bishops shall go to war and shall not perish, but shall return thence safe; afterwards", ""),
                    (20, "body", "vero illis p[ro]sp[er]a euenient. Si in: viij. nocte in illo ano domor[um] incendiu[m] ess[e] significat. Si in: ix. nocte in illo ano multi", "indeed prosperous things shall happen to them. If on the 8th night, in that year it signifies the burning of houses. If on the 9th night, in that year many", ""),
                    (21, "body", "senes morie[n]do int[er]ibu[n]t. Si in: x. nocte in illo ano multa ligna siluar[um] co[n]fringent[ur] pro ve[n]tor[um] valitudine. Si in: xj. nocte", "old men shall perish by dying. If on the 10th night, in that year many trees of the woods shall be broken by the strength of the winds. If on the 11th night,", ""),
                    (22, "body", "in illo ano multa pecora morient[ur] Si in: xij. nocte in illo ano reges ad bellu[m] ibu[n]t et in bello pugna[n]tes morie[n]do int[er]ibu[n]t.", "in that year many cattle shall die. If on the 12th night, in that year kings shall go to war and fighting in war shall perish by dying.", ""),
                    (23, "body", "¶ Si in prima die natal[is] d[omi]ni sol luce[m] videat[ur] in illo anno f[i]ni dei letab[u]nt[ur]. Si in. 2. die in illo anno aur[um] et arge[n]tu[m] habu[n]da=", "If on the first day of the Nativity of the Lord the sun is seen to shine, in that year the servants of God shall rejoice. If on the 2nd day, in that year gold and silver", "Red pilcrow '¶' at start."),
                    (24, "body", "bit multu[m]. Si in. 3. die boni er[u]nt filij hom[inum] vituli et agni. Si in: 4: die in illo ano no[n] erit bellu[m] l[a]eticia s[ed] pax et co[n]cordia.", "shall abound much. If on the 3rd day, the sons of men, calves, and lambs shall be good. If on the 4th day, in that year there shall be no war, [but] gladness, peace, and concord.", ""),
                    (25, "body", "Si in. 5. die in illo anno f[o]enu[m] m[u]ltu[m] erit in terra. Si in: 6: die arbores multitudinem gla[n]dium p[ro]creabu[n]t. Si in: 7:", "If on the 5th day, in that year there shall be much hay on the earth. If on the 6th day, trees shall bring forth a multitude of acorns. If on the 7th [day],", ""),
